WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.330
One of the most infamous moments in Game of
Thrones is the Red Wedding, when the King

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.890
in the North Robb Stark is betrayed by Walder
Frey.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:14.230
Robb is killed, along with his mother Catelyn,
and his wife Talisa in the show, and with

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.251
thousands of his men.

00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:20.140
It’s a sudden, shocking end to some of the
heroes of the series.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.490
And it’s tragic for– so many reasons.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:29.380
Robb fights so hard to rescue his father Ned
and his lost siblings, but he fails.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.520
His independent northern kingdom falls to
the treacherous Boltons.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.800
Catelyn sees her firstborn child murdered
before her eyes, and she dies believing that

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.780
Bran Rickon and Arya are also dead.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:47.760
Talisa dies along with her unborn child – though
this character’s different in the books.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.750
Arya arrives at the Twins hoping to reunite
with her family, but she only arrives in time

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.360
for them to die.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.410
The Mormonts, Manderlys, and many other northern
families lose sons, daughters, brothers and

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:05.189
sisters . And there’s another detail which
could add yet more tragedy to this massacre

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:09.380
– involving the death of the direwolf Grey
Wind.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:14.659
At the beginning of Game of Thrones, the Stark
family find some direwolf pups.

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:17.409
Direwolves are like wolves but bigger, and
more…

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:22.829
mystical . They’re also on the heraldry
of House Stark, so Ned lets each of his children

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:24.430
keep a direwolf.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.990
Robb has Grey Wind.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:27.689
Sansa has Lady.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:29.090
Arya has Nymeria.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.570
Bran has Summer.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.299
Rickon has Shaggydog.

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:34.289
And Jon has Ghost.

00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:38.670
As the story goes on, we learn that these
direwolves are more than just pets.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.689
They develop a magical connection with the
Stark kids, allowing them to feel what their

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:47.380
wolves are feeling, even to “warg” into
them – meaning they can enter the minds

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:52.740
of their wolves, and see through their eyes
. Bran does this the most, as part of his

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.310
magical journey – but the other Starks have
the same kind of power . Sansa doesn’t use

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:01.649
hers, because Lady is killed in Book 1.

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:07.399
But Arya wargs into Nymeria, even after Arya
leaves Westeros, and Nymeria becomes leader

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:08.920
of a wolf pack.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.819
Rickon and Shaggydog we don’t know much
about.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:16.970
They die in the show, but in the books they’re
apparently alive on like a cannibal unicorn

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.970
island?

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.110
that we’ll hopefully see next book.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:25.360
Jon tends to resist his power, but he does
warg Ghost sometimes , and many readers believe

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.250
that Ghost will play a role in Jon’s resurrection
in the books.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.500
There’s this whole thing about how when
wargs die, their mind can live on inside their

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.720
wolf . The character Varamyr does this in
the Prologue of Book 5 – he dies, but then

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.819
lives a “second life” as his wolf.

00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:47.659
And when Jon dies at the end of Book 5, he
might do the same thing – live on in his

00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:52.969
direwolf Ghost . Jon’s last word when he
dies is “Ghost”, and the description of

00:02:52.969 --> 00:02:58.409
“cold” in his death is similar to Varamyr’s
. Jon won’t stay in Ghost for good – Melisandre

00:02:58.409 --> 00:03:03.090
has a vision of Jon changing from “a man”
to “a wolf” to “a man again” – so

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:08.159
maybe Jon will stay in Ghost for a while,
then be resurrected as a man by Melisandre,

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:09.950
like he is in the show.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.810
Watch this video for more on book-Jon’s
resurrection.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.890
But the point is that wargs can live on in
their wolves, and some readers believe that

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.189
this happens with Robb and Grey Wind.

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:25.379
We don’t know much about Robb’s relationship
with his wolf, because like Rickon, Robb is

00:03:25.379 --> 00:03:30.180
not a POV character in the books – we don’t
see the story from his point of view.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.180
But Robb does seem close with Grey Wind.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.530
The wolf fights alongside Robb in battle , and
growls at the Freys who later betray Robb.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:42.459
But in Book 3, Robb doesn’t listen to his
wolf’s warnings.

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:46.840
He starts to distance himself from Grey Wind
– as Robb gets more involved in southern

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.760
politics, it becomes inconvenient to bring
a man-eating wolf to his meetings.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.879
So before the Red Wedding, Grey Wind is locked
up outside the feast.

00:03:55.879 --> 00:04:01.219
And this disconnection by Robb from his mystical
northern Stark roots is part of what leads

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:02.219
to his downfall.

00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:06.650
Cause when shit gets real and the Wedding
gets Red, Grey Wind isn’t there to save

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:07.650
Robb.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.640
But, Robb may return to his wolf in the end.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.499
Robb’s last words are “Grey Wind”.

00:04:13.499 --> 00:04:15.439
Just like Jon’s last word is “Ghost”.

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:21.900
So maybe like Jon and like Varamyr, Robb lives
a second life as his direwolf Grey Wind.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.590
A very short second life.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:28.960
Cause after Robb dies, the Freys also kill
Grey Wind.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.620
In the books, a Stark supporter called Raynald
Westerling briefly frees Grey Wind – and

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:39.720
the wolf attacks some Freys before being shot
down . So maybe that’s actually Robb living

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.840
through Grey Wind, attacking his Frey betrayers
before being killed again.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:50.390
Imagine how confused and angry and hurt Robb
would have been – having his family and

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:55.380
his men and himself murdered, then finding
himself in the body of his wolf for a final

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.760
frantic fight before dying a second and final
time.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.850
After Grey Wind is killed, the Freys stitch
the wolf’s head onto Robb’s corpse, which

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:11.440
is gruesome, but there’s also a neat symmetry
here – because Grey Wind’s head is on

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:17.070
Robb’s body, just as Robb’s mind wargs
into Grey Wind’s body – this might be

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:18.860
a deliberate parallel.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.870
So there’s no proof.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:25.840
But it seems very possible that Robb wargs
Grey Wind and dies twice.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.280
It doesn’t really change the plot, but it
does make Robb’s death even sadder.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:36.490
In the show, Arya sees Grey Wind die, there’s
a moment of eye contact between her and the

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:37.490
wolf.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:41.940
Which means if Robb wargs Grey Wind, he not
only sees his mother and wife and men and

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.870
himself die, he also sees his long lost sister
for the last time.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:53.060
He sees the fear and danger she’s in, but
Robb’s unable to save her – he dies powerless,

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:57.330
pained and confused, in a foreign body, in
a foreign land.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:02.160
Maybe this is punishment from the old gods
for a northerner who strayed too far south.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.080
Or maybe this isn’t really the end for Robb.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.030
If you wanna get tinfoil with this, we can
go further.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:14.260
Cause this guy Raynald Westerling – after
he frees Grey Wind, he gets shot with crossbows,

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.030
but escapes into a river.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:22.050
So it’s possible that Raynald survives . And
thing is, wargs can live a second life not

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:27.140
only in wolves, but in humans as well – in
the Prologue, Varamyr tries to take over the

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:33.190
body of a wildling called Thistle . Maybe
Robb could do the same – maybe Robb is killed

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:38.190
at the Red Wedding, then wargs into Grey Wind,
and then when the wolf dies, wargs into Raynald

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.680
Westerling, who escapes downriver.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.620
King Robb could still be alive somewhere,
in Raynald’s body – maybe to reunite with

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:50.000
his zombie mother, Stoneheart – cause Catelyn
is resurrected in the books.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.150
Maybe when Stoneheart leads a Red Wedding
revenge, Robb, as Raynald, could stab a Frey

00:06:55.150 --> 00:07:02.060
in the heart and say ‘Robb Stark sends his
regards’ – just as Roose did to Robb . But

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.420
that’s just fan fiction.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:10.580
Robb probably doesn’t warg Raynald, there
are enough resurrected Starks as it is, with

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.120
Jon and Stoneheart.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:18.740
But it is plausible that Robb wargs Grey Wind
and dies twice in one night.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:24.540
Another layer of horror and pain to the travesty
of the Red Wedding.

